{"type":"llm_response","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:40:32.709Z","data":{"turn":120,"content":"{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"So the payment webhook is confirmed to work without authentication. And the MongoDB `$where` injection is blocked by the MongoDB version being used (newer MongoDB versions disable `$where` by default). This is still an injection sink in the code, but MongoDB's built-in security prevents it from working.\\n\\nNow I have enough information to compile the full recon deliverable. Let me check one more thing - the uploads directory listing and the middleware chain.\",\"signature\":\"\"}","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:40:32.709Z"}}
{"type":"llm_response","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:40:34.104Z","data":{"turn":121,"content":"{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01NMvBygvKrjpJrHBe3LC6aL\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"curl -s http://host.docker.internal:3000/uploads/ | head -50\\necho \\\"---\\\"\\n# Check the CORS response\\ncurl -s -I -X OPTIONS http://host.docker.internal:3000/api/auth/login -H \\\"Origin: http://evil.com\\\" -H \\\"Access-Control-Request-Method: POST\\\" | head -20\",\"description\":\"Test uploads directory and CORS\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:40:34.104Z"}}
{"type":"llm_response","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:40:42.183Z","data":{"turn":122,"content":"{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Confirmed:\\n1. `/uploads/` has directory listing enabled\\n2. CORS returns any origin with credentials: `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: http://evil.com` + `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true`\\n\\nNow I have sufficient information to write the comprehensive recon deliverable. Let me structure it properly.\\n\\nKey findings summary:\\n- HireFlow is a Node.js/Express freelance marketplace\\n- Dual auth (session + JWT) with hardcoded weak secrets\\n- 77 API endpoints across 12 modules\\n- Critical SQL injection (public): GET /api/users?search=\\n\\n\\n- NoSQL injection in the gigs endpoint (though MongoDB version limits exploitation), unauthenticated payment webhooks, SSRF vulnerabilities across multiple locations, several IDOR issues in contracts and messaging, unprotected Socket.IO connections, and open CORS with directory listing on uploads.\\n\\nNow I'm ready to compile the full deliverable.\",\"signature\":\"\"}","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:40:42.183Z"}}
